=>In locally spring boot auth service running on port in prod is 8085
also in container 8085 and also exposing in browser is 8085

=>In locally postgresql running on port in prod is 5432 so let connect with docker postgresql..here no sepaate db container

note: 8083 for dev and 8085 for prod environment

🟢 Scenario A (Your current)
DB → running on your laptop (local PostgreSQL)
App → Docker container
👉 Use: host.docker.internal
👉 Docker network ❌ not needed
------------------------------------
🟢 Scenario B (Real production)
DB → Docker container
App → Docker container
👉 Use: postgres (service name)
👉 Docker Compose + Docker network ✅ required

=======================================================================
Execution flow
==================
Here i am running my spboot application inside docker but databse is my local laptop ..see the steps..
mvn clean package -DskipTests
docker build -t spboot-auth-service-img
docker run -d -p 8085:8085 -e SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=prod -e DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://host.docker.internal:5432/spboot-auth-service
-e DB_USERNAME=postgres -e DB_PASSWORD=sisu spboot-auth-service-img

